{"id": "d3a98a6c-6cc6-4b80-94a9-9504ddddb8b1", "role": "user", "content": [{"text": "[DEEP RESEARCH MODE]
{
  "task": "Read-only compliance audit of the WORKER NODES of EKS cluster 'cis-skill-test' (us-east-1, AWS account 012345678901_1). For EVERY control below return: control ID, title, status (PASS / FAIL / NOT APPLICABLE / NOT VERIFIED), and concrete evidence (API call used and the actual values observed, per node group / launch template / instance). Never assume a status; if you cannot verify, say NOT VERIFIED and why.",
  "controls": [
    "CIS Amazon EKS Benchmark v1.8.0 section 3 (Worker Nodes): 3.1.1-3.1.4 (kubeconfig / kubelet config file permissions and ownership), 3.2.1-3.2.9 (kubelet settings: anonymous auth, authorization-mode, client CA, read-only port, streaming-connection-idle-timeout, make-iptables-util-chains, eventRecordQPS, rotate-certificates, RotateKubeletServerCertificate), 3.3.1 container-optimized OS. Use the exact official v1.8.0 IDs/titles (verify with verify_aws_claim if unsure and flag uncertainty). These are host-level settings: infer from AWS-visible evidence where legitimately possible (node group AMI type e.g. AL2023/Bottlerocket/EKS-optimized AMI, launch template user data / kubelet config overrides, SSM-based inspection if SSM access is available and read-only) and otherwise mark NOT VERIFIED with the reason. Do not claim PASS from defaults without saying that is an inference and citing the AMI type and version.",
    "AWS-3 node group version support: for every managed node group (and self-managed nodes / Fargate / Karpenter nodes if present) report Kubernetes version, AMI release version, whether it matches the control plane version, and whether that Kubernetes version is still in standard/extended support as of 2026-11-19 (use verify_aws_claim for the EKS version calendar).",
    "AWS-7 node volume encryption: for every node group launch template / EC2 instance, are root and additional EBS volumes encrypted (and with which KMS key)? Also check the account/region EBS encryption-by-default setting.",
    "AWS-8 node IMDSv2: for every node group launch template / EC2 instance, HttpTokens=required? HttpPutResponseHopLimit value? HttpEndpoint status."
  ],
  "context": "Part of a full EKS compliance check requested by the user. Another sub-agent covers control plane / AWS service checks (logging, GuardDuty, CloudTrail, backup, endpoint, secrets encryption) and another covers in-cluster RBAC/pods/images; do not duplicate those. Use only read-only AWS calls. Cluster: cis-skill-test, region us-east-1, account 012345678901_1.",
  "output": "A list per control: ID | title | status | evidence. Finish with a short list of controls you could not verify and why."
}", "type": "text"}], "created_at": null}

{"id": "78fced52-60f4-411f-a2c9-e62e26084ae9", "role": "user", "content": [{"text": "[DEEP RESEARCH MODE]
{
  "task": "Read-only compliance audit of IN-CLUSTER Kubernetes policy and IMAGE controls for EKS cluster 'cis-skill-test' (us-east-1, AWS account 012345678901_1). For EVERY control below return: control ID, title, status (PASS / FAIL / NOT APPLICABLE / NOT VERIFIED), and concrete evidence (what you queried and the actual values/resources observed). Never assume a status; if you cannot verify, say NOT VERIFIED and why.",
  "controls": [
    "CIS Amazon EKS Benchmark v1.8.0 section 4 (Policies): 4.1.x RBAC and service accounts (cluster-admin use, access to secrets, wildcard use in Roles/ClusterRoles, create pods, default service accounts, SA token mounting, system:masters, bind/impersonate/escalate, and the remaining 4.1.x items in the official list), 4.2.x Pod Security Standards / admission (privileged containers, hostPID, hostIPC, hostNetwork, allowPrivilegeEscalation, root containers, NET_RAW, added capabilities, etc.), 4.3.1 CNI supports network policies, 4.3.2 all namespaces have network policies, 4.4.1 prefer secrets as files over env vars, 4.4.2 consider external secret storage, 4.5.1 use namespaces for boundaries, 4.5.2 default namespace not used. Use the exact official v1.8.0 IDs/titles (verify with verify_aws_claim if unsure; flag uncertainty). Kubernetes API data may only be reachable if this agent space has Kubernetes/EKS access configured (check associations, EKS access entries, any kubectl-like capability). AWS APIs can still show the VPC CNI add-on version/config (network policy enabled), access entries and their policies (e.g. AmazonEKSClusterAdminPolicy associations), Fargate profiles and add-ons. If in-cluster data cannot be read, mark those controls NOT VERIFIED with the precise reason; do not guess.",
    "CIS v1.8.0 section 5.1 and 5.2 (image registry & IAM for workloads): 5.1.1 image vulnerability scanning (ECR scan-on-push / enhanced scanning via Inspector), 5.1.2 minimize user access to ECR (read-only evidence: repository policies, noting you cannot change IAM), 5.1.3 minimize cluster access to read-only for ECR (node role / pod identity policies), 5.1.4 minimize container registries to only those approved (which registries do running images come from?), 5.2.1 prefer dedicated EKS service accounts (IRSA / Pod Identity associations).",
    "AWS-6 vulnerabilities in running images: determine which images are actually running in the cluster (from Kubernetes if accessible; otherwise from ECR/Inspector coverage, ECS-style task inventory is not applicable) and report Inspector (or ECR scan) findings for them: counts by severity (CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW), top CVEs with affected image/repository and fix availability. State explicitly if Inspector/ECR scanning is not enabled or if running images could not be enumerated."
  ],
  "context": "Part of a full EKS compliance check requested by the user. Another sub-agent covers control plane / AWS service checks and another covers worker node settings; do not duplicate those. Use only read-only calls. Cluster: cis-skill-test, region us-east-1, account 012345678901_1.",
  "output": "A list per control: ID | title | status | evidence. Finish with a short list of controls you could not verify and why."
}", "type": "text"}], "created_at": null}
